  "metadata": {
    "title": "Benchmark Set: Counting Minimum OCTs",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.16884175",
    "publication_date": "2025-08-15",
    "description": "<p>This benchmark contains instances of the <em>model counting problem</em> built from a graph family of (initially) constant treewidth to which <em>cardinality constraints</em> were added. The added constraints can increase the treewidth of the resulting CNFs.</p>",
